A GPG recipient, in `.vault/config`, a `wrap` rule, `--recipient` or `NIMVAULT_GPG_RECIPIENT`, must be an email address, a key ID or a fingerprint; any other string is refused when the config loads. Such a spec went to gpg as a substring, so `recipient = Alice` made `Malice <malice@example.com>` an allowed signer and a record she signed was restored by a plain `unseal`. The signer lookup no longer matches a name at all.
